    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the July 4th slate with a clear focus on aggressive base-running and high-floor matchups against shaky arms. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) headlines our lineup, benefiting from a prime matchup against Kyle Leahy; his elite sprint speed makes him our highest-ceiling play, especially with the optimizer rewarding the dynamic platoon advantage. **Christian Yelich** (75.84) and **Trea Turner** (68.32) follow closely, as both command high-leverage spots in the order against Merrill Kelly and Michael Wacha, respectively. While **Yordan Alvarez** (55.68) possesses the highest xwOBA on the roster, his score is slightly tempered by a difficult matchup against Drew Rasmussen, but his elite offensive profile necessitates his inclusion despite the sub-60 rating.\n\nWe continue to prioritize favorable platoon splits, as evidenced by the high scores for **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) and **Caleb Durbin** (63.89). **Schmitt** is particularly well-positioned today against Tomoyuki Sugano, where the combination of park factors and a favorable platoon shift elevates his utility. On the bench, **Josh Smith** (55.29) was the most difficult exclusion; he remains a viable pivot, but the optimizer favored the structural consistency of our current starting group. We are closely monitoring the 37% rain risk attached to **Chase Meidroth**, which effectively neutralized his appeal despite a decent baseline projection. Note that all lineups are currently pending, so please confirm the official batting orders for **Gary Sanchez** and **Dillon Dingler** before first pitch, as their scoring efficiency relies heavily on their projected spots in the middle-to-bottom of the order.",
